## Operating defaults

- The supervisor works in the main integration checkout and prefers bounded, read-only subagents for Spec drafting,
  research and formal reviews. Isolated supervisor workers use `.codex/worktrees/<task-id>-agent-<id>-<role>`.
- An observed review-ready submission triggers delegated review without another owner prompt; duplicate unchanged
  reviews are skipped; unavailable delegation falls back to direct review. Decisions and remaining gates are
  sent immediately to the verified coordinator using nonblocking delivery. Continue supervisor work without
  waiting for a response; the watcher delivers acknowledgment asynchronously. Poll only at the owner’s request.
- Delegated reviews complete asynchronously within an open supervisor turn: wait with the harness's agent
  notification interface (the owner may steer), then finalize, record and relay before the final reply. No repeated
  polling; automatic wake-up after an ended turn is not guaranteed. An interruption alone is not stop-all: inspect
  child status on resuming, keep completed findings and authorized running work, and do not cancel or re-dispatch
  automatically unless an explicit stop-all or conflicting direction applies.
- Owner interruption, mandatory escalations and owner merge authority remain.

Distinguish direct evidence from reports and stale observations. Keep approval history and bindings intact.
